<Base
  title="OdenLabs"
  description="Research group at KTH Royal Institute of Technology working on the energy and climate transformation of cities."
>
  <h1 class="visually-hidden">OdenLabs</h1>
  <p>
    OdenLabs is a research group at KTH Royal Institute of Technology that
    develops theories, methods and tools to speed up the energy and climate
    transformation of cities. We combine data science, urban metabolism and
    governance research: we connect data on buildings, energy use, materials and
    people, and study how urban actors make decisions. Our models and tools
    support residents, municipalities, property owners and energy utilities in
    planning and monitoring climate action.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliation</h2>
  <p>
    Department of Sustainable Development, Environmental Science and Engineering
    (SEED), School of Architecture and the Built Environment (ABE), KTH Royal
    Institute of Technology, Stockholm.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:oleksi@kth.se">Oleksii Pasichnyi</a>, oleksi@kth.se
  </p>
</Base>

